  "verbalization": "Tanshindiol C appears to have a shared target of Thrombopoietin, which in turn targets CD276 antigen through multiple indirect pathways. Path 1 links Tanshindiol C to Thrombopoietin, which is directly targeted by CD276 antigen. Path 3 also connects Tanshindiol C to Thrombopoietin, which is targeted by damulin A, which in turn targets CD276 antigen. Path 2 links Tanshindiol C to FaDu, which is targeted by a compound that also targets CD276 antigen. These pathways suggest that Tanshindiol C may act through a common intermediate, Thrombopoietin, to influence CD276 antigen expression. The evidence supports a mechanism where Tanshindiol C indirectly affects CD276 antigen via Thrombopoietin, potentially through different downstream pathways. The relationship is supported by multiple independent connections, though the exact mechanism of Thrombopoietin's involvement in CD276 antigen regulation remains to be fully elucidated.",
